1
00:04:05,945 --> 00:04:07,865
Let's go.

2
00:04:35,945 --> 00:05:05,925
We'll be right back.

3
00:05:05,945 --> 00:05:35,925
We'll be right back.

4
00:05:35,945 --> 00:05:40,005
Faded mother and daughter.

5
00:05:40,425 --> 00:05:41,985
The mother's name is Ovia.

6
00:05:50,625 --> 00:05:52,665
It's been a while, hasn't it?

7
00:05:53,065 --> 00:05:53,805
It's Ovia.

8
00:05:54,065 --> 00:05:54,945
You came back.

9
00:05:54,985 --> 00:05:57,025
We heard news that you've been captured by the Navy.

10
00:05:57,025 --> 00:05:59,185
Don't tell me you came back on their ship.

11
00:06:06,645 --> 00:06:11,765
I hate to have to tell you this as soon as I return, but the news you heard is true.

12
00:06:12,085 --> 00:06:13,045
It's not your fault.

13
00:06:13,045 --> 00:06:16,045
We knew the government would set its sights on Ohara eventually.

14
00:06:16,845 --> 00:06:22,845
I'm not sure how much you know, but the Poneglyph search team that set off six years ago was annihilated by the Marines.

15
00:06:23,285 --> 00:06:24,965
Thirty-three researchers were killed.

16
00:06:25,325 --> 00:06:27,685
I was the... the only survivor.

17
00:06:28,245 --> 00:06:30,245
Fortunately, I was only captured.

18
00:06:30,785 --> 00:06:34,825
But I overheard the Marines talking after they had rummaged through the search team's belongings.

19
00:06:34,825 --> 00:06:37,985
They soon realized that we all came from Ohara.

20
00:06:39,205 --> 00:06:40,865
I won't make any excuses.

21
00:06:41,665 --> 00:06:44,445
All of you are in danger because of my carelessness.

22
00:06:44,845 --> 00:06:45,485
Stop it.

23
00:06:45,765 --> 00:06:47,405
Thinking like that won't do any good.

24
00:06:48,245 --> 00:06:52,425
Those who set out to sea and those who stayed behind are all part of the same team.

25
00:06:52,825 --> 00:06:55,985
After what happened, if anyone should apologize, it's us.

26
00:06:56,645 --> 00:06:58,485
We know how much you've suffered.

27
00:07:00,465 --> 00:07:00,905
Professor.

28
00:07:01,665 --> 00:07:05,865
For years now, the world government has seen Ohara as a threat to their rule.

29
00:07:06,285 --> 00:07:11,525
But all we can do is believe in the truth of history and its value to all generations to come.

30
00:07:11,925 --> 00:07:15,025
Be that as it may, they've put us in quite a compromising position.

31
00:07:15,385 --> 00:07:17,545
I just don't know how we're going to get out of this one.

32
00:07:17,725 --> 00:07:19,465
I admit, it doesn't look good.

33
00:07:19,745 --> 00:07:22,425
But we're fortunate to have discovered this information when we did.

34
00:07:22,905 --> 00:07:25,705
We know that the government is hunting down all the scholars on the island.

35
00:07:26,225 --> 00:07:29,685
So before they make it to the library, we have to escape from Ohara.

36
00:07:30,345 --> 00:07:31,245
You have a point.

37
00:07:32,245 --> 00:07:36,885
This time I have a feeling we won't be able to slip past their investigation like we have before.

38
00:07:37,345 --> 00:07:40,725
And if they're committed to killing us, they won't listen to reason either.

39
00:07:41,165 --> 00:07:42,605
Then hurry up and run!

40
00:07:42,865 --> 00:07:43,945
I'm sorry, Olvia.

41
00:07:44,145 --> 00:07:48,905
I can't let myself escape and leave one of mankind's greatest treasures behind.

42
00:07:49,445 --> 00:07:50,405
You should know that.

43
00:07:50,885 --> 00:07:52,865
Everyone else here feels the same way.

44
00:07:53,025 --> 00:07:53,405
Yeah.

45
00:07:53,925 --> 00:07:54,745
Are you sure?

46
00:07:55,705 --> 00:07:58,285
We still don't know what the government's going to do when they get here.

47
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:02,085
But we do know if we run, we can't protect all this precious knowledge.

48
00:08:02,285 --> 00:08:04,005
We're not planning on dying here.

49
00:08:04,225 --> 00:08:04,825
Don't worry.

50
00:08:05,165 --> 00:08:09,845
More importantly, I know you have something else weighing on your mind.

51
00:08:10,425 --> 00:08:11,145
I can't.

52
00:08:11,585 --> 00:08:12,845
It's too late for that.

53
00:08:13,845 --> 00:08:15,385
Make up your mind, Olvia.

54
00:08:15,805 --> 00:08:17,805
Are you going to board this ship or not?

55
00:08:17,805 --> 00:08:22,185
If you want to stay with your daughter, we'll settle your husband's unfinished business for you.

56
00:08:23,185 --> 00:08:25,065
No, I'm not turning back.

57
00:08:25,545 --> 00:08:27,045
I'm a scholar of Ohara.

58
00:08:27,605 --> 00:08:31,625
It's my duty to carry out the will of those who came before me.

59
00:08:32,465 --> 00:08:33,405
Forgive me, Robin.

60
00:08:33,405 --> 00:08:38,105
I swear, I'll solve these mysteries and come back to you someday.

61
00:08:38,105 --> 00:08:44,265
Where's my mommy?

62
00:08:45,765 --> 00:08:47,025
Where'd she go?

63
00:08:47,545 --> 00:08:49,605
Your mom had to go out to sea for her job.

64
00:08:50,025 --> 00:08:52,185
You'll be staying here with us for a little while, okay?

65
00:08:52,645 --> 00:08:53,505
That's enough.

66
00:08:53,565 --> 00:08:54,985
If you don't shut up, I'll hit you.

67
00:08:55,065 --> 00:08:55,945
Honey, stop it.

68
00:08:55,985 --> 00:08:56,925
She's only two.

69
00:08:57,185 --> 00:08:58,305
And so is our daughter.

70
00:08:58,865 --> 00:09:00,945
Listen, I don't care if she's your sister's child.

71
00:09:00,945 --> 00:09:01,665
She's a burden.

72
00:09:02,105 --> 00:09:03,265
This was a mistake.

73
00:09:08,585 --> 00:09:09,465
Who's there?

74
00:09:09,565 --> 00:09:10,845
What are you doing here?

75
00:09:13,365 --> 00:09:16,485
Uh, I was, I, I mean, I just, uh.

76
00:09:19,245 --> 00:09:20,585
I'm so sorry.

77
00:09:23,045 --> 00:09:26,365
If you want to read a book, all you have to do is ask, all right?

78
00:09:26,585 --> 00:09:29,445
But I can't because I don't have any money.

79
00:09:29,445 --> 00:09:33,785
Well, then looks like you're in luck because you can read everything here for free.

80
00:09:34,025 --> 00:09:34,605
For free?

81
00:09:34,725 --> 00:09:35,145
Uh-huh.

82
00:09:35,345 --> 00:09:38,265
After all, this library is the best in the world.

83
00:09:38,425 --> 00:09:39,365
It is? Really?

84
00:09:39,485 --> 00:09:40,165
Sure is.

85
00:09:40,305 --> 00:09:40,925
Let's see.

86
00:09:41,165 --> 00:09:43,205
Unless I'm mistaken, you're Olvia's daughter.

87
00:09:44,465 --> 00:09:45,625
You like to read books?

88
00:09:46,185 --> 00:09:46,545
Mm-hmm.

89
00:09:48,705 --> 00:09:51,665
She looks just like you did when you were that age.

90
00:09:52,005 --> 00:09:54,925
And I'm proud to say she's every bit as clever, too.

91
00:09:55,745 --> 00:09:57,845
If she's safe, that's enough.

92
00:09:57,845 --> 00:10:02,545
When I decided to join you, I severed all bonds with her.

93
00:10:03,385 --> 00:10:05,825
I can't let her become the daughter of a criminal.

94
00:10:07,105 --> 00:10:08,005
Bad news!

95
00:10:08,265 --> 00:10:10,845
Another ship came with the world government's flag!

96
00:10:10,945 --> 00:10:14,225
One of their high-ranked officials coming all the way here to the West Blue?

97
00:10:14,745 --> 00:10:15,385
My goodness.

98
00:10:16,385 --> 00:10:18,485
It seems this is quite serious indeed.

99
00:10:18,485 --> 00:10:22,165
All right, everyone, listen.

100
00:10:22,405 --> 00:10:25,485
From now on, you and I are neither colleagues nor acquaintances.

101
00:10:27,305 --> 00:10:29,645
You have to stick to that no matter what.

102
00:10:30,545 --> 00:10:31,025
Farewell!

103
00:10:31,485 --> 00:10:32,505
Olvia, wait!

104
00:10:32,765 --> 00:10:34,105
What are you going to do?

105
00:10:34,505 --> 00:10:35,185
All right.

106
00:10:35,565 --> 00:10:37,065
Tell HQ we've arrived.

107
00:10:38,365 --> 00:10:39,205
Let's move it.

108
00:10:39,205 --> 00:10:40,745
I want to get this over with.

109
00:10:41,965 --> 00:10:43,205
What a pain.

110
00:10:44,905 --> 00:10:47,945
They better give me a promotion when this crap is over.

111
00:10:48,445 --> 00:10:48,745
Hey!

112
00:10:49,145 --> 00:10:52,225
I want you to hunt down every scholar on the island and restrain them.

113
00:10:52,425 --> 00:10:53,125
Yes, sir!

114
00:10:53,425 --> 00:10:54,445
What's going on?

115
00:10:54,505 --> 00:10:56,605
Some woman is running around with a gun!

116
00:10:56,605 --> 00:11:17,665
This is an awful mess.

117
00:11:17,965 --> 00:11:19,725
I'm sorry, Robin.

118
00:11:20,685 --> 00:11:21,865
Vice Admiral Kuzan.

119
00:11:22,365 --> 00:11:23,605
What is it?

120
00:11:23,605 --> 00:11:27,185
We've been informed that CP-9's Chief Spondyne has arrived at Ohara.

121
00:11:27,885 --> 00:11:28,765
So what?

122
00:11:29,205 --> 00:11:31,145
Did you really have to wake me up?

123
00:11:31,585 --> 00:11:33,405
Just to tell me that?

124
00:11:33,525 --> 00:11:34,325
I'm sorry, sir!

125
00:11:34,325 --> 00:11:55,985
What's the matter, Robin?

126
00:11:55,985 --> 00:12:00,005
You have to tell me, didn't my mom come by here?

127
00:12:00,965 --> 00:12:02,365
Now hold on a minute.

128
00:12:02,525 --> 00:12:03,745
Where did that come from?

129
00:12:03,745 --> 00:12:05,945
Why would you think your mother was back in Ohara?

130
00:12:07,065 --> 00:12:08,545
I've severed all bonds.

131
00:12:08,805 --> 00:12:11,825
No matter what, I can't let her become the daughter of a criminal.

132
00:12:13,085 --> 00:12:15,405
I wish she was here too, but she's not.

133
00:12:16,705 --> 00:12:17,445
Oh yeah!

134
00:12:17,725 --> 00:12:18,485
We're in trouble!

135
00:12:18,785 --> 00:12:21,525
I heard there are navy battleships coming to the island right now!

136
00:12:21,705 --> 00:12:23,805
They're trying to get rid of all the scholars on Ohara!

137
00:12:24,045 --> 00:12:26,705
The people in town must be stirring up bad rumors.

138
00:12:26,705 --> 00:12:32,505
The truth is, that's no battleship, and they won't be getting rid of anyone.

139
00:12:32,665 --> 00:12:35,045
The government is paying us a visit, though.

140
00:12:35,245 --> 00:12:38,165
And that means the library will be under an investigation.

141
00:12:38,465 --> 00:12:39,305
A harsh one.

142
00:12:39,665 --> 00:12:40,465
So listen up.

143
00:12:40,725 --> 00:12:42,985
No matter what those government agents say or do,

144
00:12:43,105 --> 00:12:47,145
you absolutely cannot let them know that you're an archaeologist like the rest of us.

145
00:12:47,145 --> 00:12:51,065
Since you're so young, as long as you keep quiet, no one will think you're a scholar.

146
00:12:51,305 --> 00:12:51,845
You understand?

147
00:12:54,145 --> 00:12:54,805
Move it!

148
00:12:56,805 --> 00:12:57,805
Stop what you're doing!

149
00:12:57,965 --> 00:12:59,765
Put your hands in the air and go outside!

150
00:13:00,485 --> 00:13:02,445
Don't you think you're being a bit violent?

151
00:13:02,945 --> 00:13:08,305
The researchers here at the Tree of Knowledge are being charged with the heinous crime of deciphering poneglyphs.

152
00:13:08,425 --> 00:13:12,105
We'll be investigating the library, so everyone get out of our way and leave the building.

153
00:13:12,605 --> 00:13:14,505
You'd better treat this place with care.

154
00:13:14,805 --> 00:13:18,665
The value of this collection is well beyond your imagination, I assure you.

155
00:13:18,725 --> 00:13:20,625
I don't have to listen to a word you say.

156
00:13:21,085 --> 00:13:21,885
Take him outside!

157
00:13:22,045 --> 00:13:22,705
Yes, sir!

158
00:13:23,485 --> 00:13:25,105
Attention, citizens of Ohara!

159
00:13:25,105 --> 00:13:31,045
I regret to inform you that the scholars of this island may be devils in disguise plotting to destroy the world.

160
00:13:31,045 --> 00:13:32,625
What? But why?

161
00:13:32,765 --> 00:13:34,945
Our scholars are the pride of every person in Ohara!

162
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:37,225
They would never dream of doing something like that!

163
00:13:37,385 --> 00:13:41,445
From this point forward, we will be conducting a large-scale search of the entire island.

164
00:13:41,745 --> 00:13:46,165
During that time, all those who are not related to the research center must take a form of identification

165
00:13:46,165 --> 00:13:49,245
and head to the evacuation ship on the west seashore.

166
00:13:49,865 --> 00:13:51,265
Evacuation? That's ridiculous!

167
00:13:51,465 --> 00:13:55,425
Even if the scholars did do something wrong that still has nothing to do with us,

168
00:13:55,745 --> 00:13:57,305
you can't kick us off our own island!

169
00:13:57,665 --> 00:14:00,705
Our only obligation was to pass on this message to you.

170
00:14:01,045 --> 00:14:07,905
Disregard our warning if you like, but we won't be held responsible should any unfortunate accidents occur.

171
00:14:13,905 --> 00:14:14,925
You heard him?

172
00:14:14,985 --> 00:14:16,905
Yeah, everyone! Back to the west shore!

173
00:14:16,965 --> 00:14:18,665
I don't want to have any part of this mess!

174
00:14:18,665 --> 00:14:25,985
I've been shot! This is it for me!

175
00:14:26,205 --> 00:14:28,245
I'm a gunner, damn it! A gunner!

176
00:14:28,485 --> 00:14:29,625
Contact the higher-ups!

177
00:14:29,905 --> 00:14:32,445
Tell them I want my son to take over for me!

178
00:14:32,525 --> 00:14:34,185
Calm down, Chief. Just take a look.

179
00:14:34,345 --> 00:14:36,165
The bullet went through your sleeve, that's all.

180
00:14:36,705 --> 00:14:37,885
Oh, I see.

181
00:14:37,885 --> 00:14:42,745
I'll aim to kill next time.

182
00:14:42,745 --> 00:14:44,745
Well, if it isn't Nico Olvia.

183
00:14:44,745 --> 00:14:52,125
I find it hard to believe that a devious criminal like you would end up on this island completely by coincidence after your daring escape.

184
00:14:52,545 --> 00:14:56,765
In other words, despite the fact that you've denied your connection to the scholars of Ohara,

185
00:14:57,005 --> 00:15:01,025
you've shown up at their doorstep just in time to warn them of our little investigation.

186
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:06,285
Now, in my humble opinion, that very clearly labels them as your partners in crime.

187
00:15:06,285 --> 00:15:10,145
You've no idea why I'm here. That doesn't prove one single thing.

188
00:15:10,365 --> 00:15:14,325
Hmm. I'm sure you've cooked up plenty of excuses to cover for them.

189
00:15:14,545 --> 00:15:16,445
You're a clever woman, after all.

190
00:15:16,805 --> 00:15:21,705
But that doesn't really matter, because we don't have to prove your connection to the Ohara scholars anymore.

191
00:15:22,265 --> 00:15:25,125
Now that we're here, we can search every little nook and cranny.

192
00:15:25,325 --> 00:15:28,905
I doubt it'll take long before we find evidence of their poneglyph research.

193
00:15:29,525 --> 00:15:33,045
The government's quite confident in this, and you know they're never wrong.

194
00:15:33,405 --> 00:15:35,845
This has been in the works for a long time.

195
00:15:36,305 --> 00:15:40,625
Capturing you after six years of hide-and-seek was nothing more than the final push.

196
00:15:41,265 --> 00:15:44,065
There are plenty of poneglyph researchers around the world,

197
00:15:44,265 --> 00:15:48,565
and each time we captured one, we tried to find any connection they might have to Ohara.

198
00:15:49,705 --> 00:15:51,185
Can you guess why that is?

199
00:15:52,105 --> 00:15:54,685
Don't tell me. You're making an example of us?

200
00:15:54,865 --> 00:16:01,285
Exactly. If we crush this holy ground of archaeology, the entire academic world will take notice.

201
00:16:01,285 --> 00:16:07,005
It's the perfect opportunity to show the world exactly what happens to those who research the blank century.

202
00:16:07,005 --> 00:16:11,425
Then, the battleships from headquarters waiting on standby are here, too.

203
00:16:12,065 --> 00:16:15,605
Well, look at that. You are a clever woman, aren't you?

204
00:16:15,605 --> 00:16:20,445
Yes, as you might guess, there to ensure that not even a single criminal escapes.

205
00:16:21,245 --> 00:16:24,865
However, as a matter of form, we still need to verify their guilt.

206
00:16:25,165 --> 00:16:26,985
We aren't pirates, after all.

207
00:16:27,325 --> 00:16:31,185
So I came all this way to conduct a compulsory investigation of the island

208
00:16:31,185 --> 00:16:33,705
and chase off anyone who's not involved.

209
00:16:34,085 --> 00:16:35,905
It's curtains for you and your friends.

210
00:16:36,285 --> 00:16:37,585
There's no escape.

211
00:16:37,585 --> 00:16:40,205
Take her down.

212
00:16:51,985 --> 00:16:55,005
Hey, what are you doing? All the books here are world treasures.

213
00:16:55,325 --> 00:16:57,005
Take them outside and shut them up.

214
00:16:57,065 --> 00:16:57,765
Move it!

215
00:16:58,005 --> 00:16:59,085
You bastards!

216
00:16:59,245 --> 00:17:01,405
They must have a secret room somewhere around here.

217
00:17:01,565 --> 00:17:03,125
Don't stop until you find it!

218
00:17:07,585 --> 00:17:09,425
This is worse than I thought!

219
00:17:10,205 --> 00:17:13,765
The battleships are here already and there's a whole mess of them!

220
00:17:15,905 --> 00:17:17,205
That should be everyone!

221
00:17:17,845 --> 00:17:19,525
Good! Now don't let them go anywhere!

222
00:17:21,205 --> 00:17:23,145
Look, they're rounding up all the scholars!

223
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:24,565
What did they do wrong?

224
00:21:55,113 --> 00:22:25,093
We'll be right back.

225
00:22:25,113 --> 00:22:55,093
We'll be right back.

226
00:22:55,113 --> 00:22:57,313
What about you, Mom? Aren't you coming with me?

227
00:22:57,753 --> 00:23:00,733
I'm afraid there's still something that I have to do here.

228
00:23:00,833 --> 00:23:02,473
No, I don't want to lose you.

229
00:23:02,813 --> 00:23:04,833
I want to stay together from now on.

230
00:23:04,933 --> 00:23:05,293
Please.

231
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:09,233
On the next, One Piece, the tragedy of Ohara,

232
00:23:09,593 --> 00:23:11,273
the terror of the Buster Call,

233
00:23:11,593 --> 00:23:13,333
I'm going to be king of the pirates.

